    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 122155\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n255 PM PDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Breezy south-southwesterly wind gusts will continue through the\n  week with dry conditions and near-normal temperatures.\n\n&&\n\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Friday.\n\nA closed area of low pressure is pushing into the Pacific Northwest \nthis weekend, which will result in the associated trough axis \npushing through the southern Great Basin this weekend. As a result, \nexpect elevated south-southwesterly winds with gust speeds generally \nbetween 25 and 35 mph, with occasional instances of gusts around 40 \nmph in the higher terrain. Generalized troughing will continue over \nthe region through the first half of the week, which will return \nafternoon breezes each day and bring temperatures back to within a \nfew degrees of seasonal normals. Due to the persistent dry \nconditions, a Red Flag Warning is in effect through the remainder of \nthe day for our northwestern zones. Please see the FIRE WEATHER \nsection below for more information. The monsoonal high pressure over \nthe southern United States will shift westward for the second half \nof the week, which will set up a favored flow for moisture to surge \nup the Colorado River Valley into our forecast area. That said, only \nabout half of the ECMWF and GFS ensemble members indicate a moisture \nresurgence worth noting, so confidence in resultant precipitation \nchances is low. \n&&\n\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 18Z Forecast Package... \nBreezy south to southwest winds are expected through the \nafternoon. Gusts over 20KT are likely (80% chance) with a low \nchance (20%) for gusts over 25KT. South winds will diminish after \nsunset slightly but will gust through most of the night. Similar \nwinds are expected Sunday with south to southwest winds gusting \nover 20KT Sunday late morning and afternoon. Dry conditions with \nVFR skies persisting through the period. Temperatures will exceed \n100 degrees between 20Z and 02Z today and Sunday.\n  \nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Breezy south to \nsouthwest winds are expected through the afternoon with widespread \ngusts 20-30KT. KDAG will see a lag in gusts, not seeing gusts \ndevelop until around 00Z. Winds will drop back this evening but will \nremain elevated in many locations overnight as south winds over 10KT \npersist through the night. The exception will be the Colorado River \nValley where light south to southeast winds are expected after 09Z. \nSimilar winds are expected on Sunday as southerly to southwesterly \ngusts develop late morning and continue through the afternoon. VFR \nskies with no precipitation expected through the period. \n&&\n\n\n.FIRE WEATHER...A Red Flag Warning continues for Esmeralda, southern \nNye, southwestern Lincoln, and Clark counties through 12 AM / \nMidnight tonight. Afternoon relative humidities will range from the \nupper-single-digits to lower-teens across the southwestern Great \nBasin and central Mojave Deserts today. Meanwhile, expect south-\nsouthwest winds between 15 and 25 mph with gusts to 35 mph. Cannot \nrule out occasional gusts to 40 mph in the higher terrain. Winds \ndecrease overnight and relative humidities recover between 30 and 40 \npercent. Considered a Red Flag Warning for Sunday, but the locations \nwith combined dry conditions (15 percent RH or lower) and elevated \nwinds will be isolated in time and space. That said, caution is \nencouraged when recreating with sparks or flames.\n&&\n\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Soulat\nAVIATION...Nickerson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
